current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:552966e0258997958a3a7ef72577ae4e6aff785c68534777dedd54e633334b7a","file":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":58,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"c92f487984e86bd68750a8b9e939dbd47e3621d4956a79e6e54848d4ed91f668","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:552966e0258997958a3a7ef72577ae4e6aff785c68534777dedd54e633334b7a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L58"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $G$ be an infinite connected locally finite quasi-transitive graph\nwith $h_V(G)>0$. For Bernoulli bond percolation on $G$,\n\\[\n \\sup_{0\\le p<\\pc}\\norm{T_p}_{2\\to2}\n       =\\norm{T_{\\pc}}_{2\\to2}<\\infty,\n \\qquad \\pc(G)<\\ptwo(G)\\le\\pu(G).\n\\]\nThere exist $\\pc<p_1<p_2<1$ such that, in the coupling obtained from\nindependent uniform edge labels, almost surely there are infinitely\nmany infinite open clusters simultaneously for every $p\\in[p_1,p_2]$."}
